From 09949da81e6d18876d1dd2cbc0df5edd97669f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR-Vensuki <260785366+LR-Vensuki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:29:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SWGL pixel shading on OpenGL ES 2 for legacy iOS
 (LF_SWGL_GPU=1)

gpu_gles2.h does for an OpenGL ES 2 GPU what gpu_d3d11.h does for
Direct3D 9_3: WebRender's vertex shaders stay on SWGL's CPU path, the
quads and varyings go to the GPU, which shades them with the GLSL ES
fragment shaders compiled on the device. Compositor tiles are drawn on
the GPU through textures over their IOSurfaces (EAGLContext's iOS 5-10
texImageIOSurface), and the GPU is finished before Core Animation shows
them. Also: glsl-to-cxx lowers a switch case that ends in return, which
ps_text_run's GPU variant has.
